{
  "version": 1,
  "claim": "Replacing the classical leave-one-sweep-out jackknife spread in autocal/anchor_uncertainty.py with a robust (median-based) spread over the same folds removes false 'poor quality' labels on HP5/HP5r free-low-z fits (6 -> 2 'poor' among 26 fits <=1.5 mm true error) without hiding bad fits (0 of 10 fits >5 mm labelled better than poor; lowest value on >10 mm failures 12.4 mm) and improves Spearman vs true error 0.60 -> 0.67 over 41 cases.",
  "scope": "Simulation only; 17 live runs plus noisy, disturbed and truncated reference datasets; thresholds unchanged. Also: HP4 A+10 mm live 1.04 mm; top-line off-plumb 50 mm -> <=0.09 mm offline.",
  "limitations": [
    "The spread also feeds fit selection and patience ranking; runs ending on patience untested",
    "Still over-reports ~2x on HP5",
    "'Seeds' are distinct machines (low anchors moved ±20 mm in xy), not simulator seeds"
  ],
  "candidate_revision": "e292f73e2ab2913bc36343f141fb93817b360d9f",
